Every meaningful change must improve future work.

MANDATORY DOC UPDATES (same diff) when:
- You fixed a bug (any runtime/TS/build issue)
- You discovered a new failure mode (e.g. RLS 403, infinite loading, server/client client mixup)
- You changed generator patterns or added new module scaffolding
- You changed cross-module business logic (schema, RPC, shared data access)

Update at least ONE of:
- `docs/ai/ERROR_FIX_LOG.md` (for bug fixes)
- `docs/ai/GENERATOR_RULES.md` + `docs/ai/CHANGE_CHECKLIST.md` (for scaffolding & prevention)
- `docs/ai/CROSS_MODULE_IMPACT_TEMPLATE.md` (for impact mapping baseline)

Every code change MUST also update `docs/ai/CHANGE_CHECKLIST.md` § **Target Output Verification Gate** with commands run, expected vs actual, and PASS/FAIL (Rule 43).

ENTRY TEMPLATE (copy/paste)
## YYYY-MM-DD — <short title>
- Symptom:
- Root cause:
- Fix:
- Prevention update (what rule/generator/checklist changed so this doesn't repeat):
- Files touched:
- Verification (commands + expected result + **PASS/FAIL** — Rule 43 / `docs/ai/TARGET_OUTPUT_VERIFICATION.md`):

If the fix implies a generator should scaffold something differently, update `GENERATOR_RULES.md` (not only the log).
